  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-(x-2)(x-4)>0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-(x-2)(x-4)\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/dc39c970e292e38519e609367c9f4a3d810aaca99e7040bb6227ff45401b2efc.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $2<x<4.$",
